&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Great AI doesn’t start with a great model. It starts with a great platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The success of an AI initiative is rarely determined by the model alone. More often, it depends on the quality of the platform underneath it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Platform Engineer in our central Data &amp;amp; AI team, you’ll build the foundations that let engineers develop, deploy and operate AI workloads safely and efficiently. You’ll work on the infrastructure, automation and platform capabilities that allow teams to innovate without compromising reliability, and you’ll bridge the gap between promising technology and production reality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Think Kubernetes platforms, deployment automation, observability, security and developer experience. Think AI workloads built around Large Language Models, retrieval systems, graph technologies and modern data platforms. Think creating an environment where engineers focus on solving problems rather than fighting infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will work on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing self-service platform capabilities using Kubernetes, Terraform and GitOps principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalizing graph and vector databases, and enabling model serving workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the observability of AI systems running in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrating OpenAI or Anthropic-based services into our platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalizing LangGraph workloads on Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enabling GraphRAG architectures powered by Neo4j&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing deployment patterns so AI services meet the same standards as any other production workload&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll spend less time tuning models and more time making sure AI capabilities can be trusted, operated and continuously improved. This role sits at the intersection of platform engineering, software engineering and AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Schuberg Philis we don’t believe in throwing solutions over the fence. The engineers building systems are responsible for running them too, and that ownership extends to AI just as much as every other technology we work with. Your impact won’t be measured by the number of clusters you manage, but by how much autonomy and confidence other engineers gain from the platform you’ve built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’d love to meet you if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care deeply about building platforms that other engineers love to use, and you’re happiest when automation replaces repetitive work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong background in Platform Engineering, SRE, infrastructure or distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have extensive experience building and operating Kubernetes-based and cloud-native environments, with infrastructure automation at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve built and operated production environments using tools such as Terraform, ArgoCD, GitHub Actions or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand what it takes to operationalize AI workloads in production, and technologies such as OpenAI, Anthropic, Neo4j, GraphRAG, vector databases or LangGraph are familiar territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You believe observability, reliability and security belong in every design conversation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy improving developer experience through automation and self-service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You see the gap between a successful proof of concept and a production-ready system and immediately start figuring out how to close it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take ownership of the result&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You get satisfaction from enabling other engineers to move faster and safer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are currently based in the Netherlands.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Questions? Please do not hesitate to contact Maggie: 0623757086&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Only applications submitted through the website will be considered.&amp;nbsp;Please note that we do not work with external recruitment agencies and we will not pay any fees for unrequested CV introductions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Everyone we work with and consider working with has a right to equal treatment. The hiring and appraisal process at Schuberg Philis is designed to be thorough and equitable, implementing fair payment, benefits, and opportunities across all demographics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;It is our desire to be a company that brings together multiple nationalities, cultures, religions, genders, abilities, and talents within and across our teams. We welcome colleagues from diverse backgrounds to join Schuberg Philis and actively support diversity and inclusion in the tech industry.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer at Auterion, you will play a pivotal role in the successful development, integration and deployment of Auterion-powered drone systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will collaborate closely with the production, hardware engineering, and firmware/software teams, as well as operations, ensuring that every platform transitions smoothly from an airframe concept into a fully validated flying robot ready for deployment. You will serve as the primary technical interface for partners, work closely with them to understand their technical requirements, configure and adapt existing solutions, contribute to core software development, and ensure successful implementation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for an engineer who enjoys combining hands-on technical work with customer collaboration and system-level problem solving, bridging the gap between hardware, firmware, and real-world flight performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate in a highly hands-on environment with evolving system requirements, rapidly iterating across hardware and software integration challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage software releases and perform firmware flashing and configuration using PX4 or adjacent autopilot ecosystems, including sensor calibration, ESC tuning, and system bring-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide deep avionics and airframe expertise, including autopilot tuning, sensor and payload integration, power systems and airworthiness considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work independently to troubleshoot integration and flight-readiness issues while collaborating cross-functionally with hardware engineering, firmware/software teams, operations, and QC engineering to escalate complex challenges when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary technical authority in customer engagements, translating mission requirements into concrete system architectures and demonstrable solutions built on AuterionOS and Skynode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in flight testing activities to validate platform stability, safety, and mission performance, resolving technical issues often directly in the field during customer trials and demonstrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to technical documentation and continuous improvement of engineering processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed customer and market requirements back into product and engineering teams to influence the roadmap of the Auterion stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Software, Electrical, Mechanical, Aerospace or Robotics Engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working proficiency in C/C++ and Python: you can read, debug and patch existing code and write small tools and scripts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in Linux environments, including the command line, logs, Docker and basic networking (IP, TCP/UDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on hardware-software integration: system bring-up, wiring and connectors, and embedded interfaces (UART, CAN, I2C, SPI) at a practical level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured troubleshooting: you can isolate whether a problem is software, hardware, configuration or RF, often under time pressure in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator: you can explain technical issues clearly to customers and operators, and report findings back to engineering in a way they can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to travel and work on-site with customers, including at test ranges and in field environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship (required for security clearance and customer requirements)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
